    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "Why are the older leaves on my areca palm turning yellow?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Yellowing that starts on the oldest, lowest areca palm fronds can be potassium deficiency. UF/IFAS says older leaves on areca palms often turn yellow from a lack of potassium, and the leaves are often speckled with bronze or yellow. Potassium deficiency is less common in pots than in sandy garden soil. A healthy old frond dies quickly, from green to brown in a few days; old fronds that stay half-yellow for months usually lack potassium (UF/IFAS)."
     }
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "Why is my areca palm turning yellow with wet soil?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Yellow areca palm fronds with soil that stays wet mean the roots are getting too much water. Root rot organisms thrive in wet, poorly drained potting mix (Iowa State Extension), and rotting roots cannot take up water, so the palm yellows and wilts."
     }
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "Why are my areca palm leaf tips turning brown?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Brown leaf tips on an areca palm come from dry air, a lack of water or too much fertiliser (Clemson Extension). Salts from water and fertiliser that build up in the pot cause it too (Colorado State Extension)."
     }
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "What is the fine webbing on my areca palm?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Fine webbing and pale, speckled fronds on an areca palm are spider mites. Clemson Extension says areca palms are very susceptible to spider mites, and that mites are often a problem indoors because of low humidity and warm temperatures."
     }
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "Why are my areca palm fronds sticky with black marks?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Sticky areca palm fronds with small brown or white bumps are a sign of scale insects, and the black film that follows is sooty mould growing on the sticky residue. UF/IFAS lists scale followed by sooty mould as a problem for areca palms; mealybugs also attack palms (Clemson)."
     }
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "Why is my areca palm pale or yellow in a sunny spot?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "An areca palm that turns pale yellow or bleached in a sunny spot is getting too much direct sun. UF/IFAS says young areca palms in full sun develop yellow leaves, and that the yellowing can be reduced with shade."
     }
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "Why are my areca palm fronds drooping?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Drooping or wilting areca palm fronds mean the palm is short of water. Either the soil has dried out, or rotting roots can no longer take water up. Iowa State Extension warns that root rot is often mistaken for a lack of water, so check the soil before you water."
     }
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "Why does my areca palm have brown patches after a cold night?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Reddish-brown dead areas that appear on the fronds a few days after a cold night are chilling damage (Clemson Extension). Clemson says most houseplant palms need temperatures above 7 °C (45 °F) to prevent chilling damage. In the UAE this happens outdoors inland, in the mountains and in colder GCC cities, and rarely on the coast."
     }
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "Can an areca palm live outside in the UAE?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Yes, an areca palm can live outside in the UAE in shade or partial shade. From May to September protect it from the midday and afternoon sun, because summer nights stay hot and pots dry out very fast. Move it outside gradually, not straight from an AC room. On the coast winter is mild, but inland and in colder GCC cities protect it on nights below 7 °C."
     }
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "Does an areca palm clean the air?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "An areca palm does not noticeably clean the air in a normal room. Chamber studies found that plants remove some chemicals, but a 2019 review (Cummings and Waring) showed that a home would need far more plants than anyone keeps to match normal ventilation. Choose an areca palm for its looks and because it is safe for pets."
     }
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "How fast does an areca palm grow indoors?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Clemson Extension says areca palms grow about 15–25 cm (6–10 inches) a year and reach about 1.8–2.1 m (6–7 feet) indoors, so they often outgrow their space. In their native habitat in Madagascar they can reach about 9 m (30 feet)."
     }
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "Is an areca palm the same as a bamboo palm?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "No, but the names overlap. NC State Extension and UF/IFAS list \"bamboo palm\" as a common name for the areca palm, because its clustered stems have rings like bamboo. The name is also used for two Chamaedorea palms, Chamaedorea seifrizii and the parlour palm (Chamaedorea elegans), which NC State notes are often confused with the areca palm. Both Chamaedorea palms tolerate lower light than an areca palm."
     }
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "Can I cut back an areca palm that is too tall?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "No. New growth comes from a high central growing point, so palms cannot be pruned back to reduce their height (Clemson Extension). Remove only completely dead fronds, give the palm more room, or divide a crowded clump."
     }
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "Does an areca palm flower indoors?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Rarely. NC State Extension says areca palms will rarely bloom or produce fruit as a houseplant. Outdoors, mature palms produce hanging sprays of small flowers, followed by small egg-shaped fruits (NC State Extension, UF/IFAS)."
     }
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "Is an areca palm safe around young children?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "NC State Extension rates the areca palm as a low-severity poison for people: the heart-of-palm is cyanogenic and can cause nausea and vomiting if eaten. Do not let young children chew the plant, and call your doctor or a poison centre if a child eats part of it."
     }
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "Where does the areca palm come from?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "The areca palm is native to eastern Madagascar, where UF/IFAS says it is endangered in the wild because its habitat is being lost. NC State Extension calls it one of the most popular indoor palms."
     }
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "How is plant size measured?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Size is measured from the bottom of the nursery pot to the top tip of the highest leaf. A plant listed as 50-60 CM stands in that range measured this way."
     }
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "Which pot option should I choose, nursery or decorative?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Choose the nursery pot for the lowest price or if you already have a planter. Choose a decorative pot for a ready-to-display plant that arrives fully potted with soil mix, perlite and a drainage layer. The plant itself is the same."
     }
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "Do the decorative pots have drainage holes?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Decorative pot orders include a drainage layer at the base, with premium soil mix and perlite. For specific details on a particular pot model, send us the product link and our team will confirm."
     }
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "Is the plant healthy on arrival? Can I check first?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Plants are guaranteed to arrive healthy. Check your plant with the delivery agent: if it's damaged or not what you ordered, you can refuse it on the spot. If you find damage after unpacking, send photos and your order number on WhatsApp (+971 4 294 1422) or email sales@plantsworld.ae within 24 hours and we'll replace it free. You can also ask for a pre-dispatch photo."
     }
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "My plant arrived with a few drooping or yellow leaves. Is that normal?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Yes, that's normal. A few drooping, bent or yellow leaves are a common reaction to the journey and a new spot, and plants usually recover within a few days. Keep it in bright indirect light and check the soil before watering. If the plant or pot is actually damaged, send photos within 24 hours."
     }
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "Will my plant be safe in the UAE heat during delivery?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Yes. Our own delivery team brings your order, not a third-party courier. In extreme summer heat (June to September) we may move deliveries to farther emirates to a cooler day and agree the new day with you. If anything arrives damaged, we replace it free."
     }
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "Will my plant look exactly like the website photo?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "You'll receive the variety and size you ordered, but every plant grows individually, so leaf count, shape and shade can differ from the photo, which is representative. For peace of mind, ask for a pre-dispatch photo at checkout or on WhatsApp."
     }
    }
   ]
